==Battleground==
*1 [[Cruel Angel Clionel]] spawns as the boss after 5 seconds<sup>150f</sup>.
*1 [[Hannya]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 20~40 seconds<sup>600f~1,200f</sup>.
*2 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*4 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn after 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>, delay 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Cruel Angel Clionel and Hannya are a deadly combo, with Hannya attacking cats within Clionel's blindspot and weakening anything that survives. However, [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]] can be used to stall the duo, fitting within Clionel's blindspot and tanking lots of damage from Hannya, though dying quickly to the Doge Darks and Gory Darks. If you happen to have her, [[Rei Ayanami (???) (Super Rare Cat)|Rei Ayanami (???)]] may be more useful than Roe, who tanks damage from the peons much better but takes a bit more damage from Hannya.

Rushers such as [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] can be used to deal with the peons, but may not be enough, with Anti-Dark units such as [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Assassin BearCat]] or [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] being useful for clean-up. It is worth mentioning that Bullet Train, when true formed at level 50, is capable of one-shotting Doge Dark with any Attack Up combo. [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]] is especially useful, one-shotting the Gories, and being able to deal good damage to Hannya, do note though, Yukimura will not be able to survive a hit from Hannya or Clionel.

The [[Sniper the Cat|Sniper]] consumable and [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Recruit]] are very useful for keeping Clionel away from the base. This can also nudge Clionel behind Hannya to get damage in with rushers.

